# Real-World Projects

Every project a portfolio needs, distilled to a one-liner + the core layout pattern. Use these as blueprints; each maps back to everything you've built.

---

## 1. Personal portfolio
**Hero + projects grid + about + contact; single-page, scroll-anchored.**
```tsx
<main className="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-24 py-16">
  <Hero /><Projects /><About /><Contact />
</main>
```

## 2. Blog
**Index + slug route; typography-driven article pages.**
```
app/
├── blog/page.tsx              → grid of posts
└── blog/[slug]/page.tsx       → prose article
```
```tsx
<article className="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <h1>{post.title}</h1>
  <p>{post.excerpt}</p>
</article>
```

## 3. Login page
**Centered card, email + password, social auth, forgot link.**
```tsx
<div className="min-h-screen grid place-items-center p-4 bg-slate-100">
  <div className="w-full max-w-md rounded-3xl bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
    <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Welcome back</h1>
    {/* fields + button */}
  </div>
</div>
```

## 4. Registration page
**Same shell as login; more fields + password strength + terms.**
```tsx
<form className="space-y-5">
  <TextField label="Name" />
  <TextField label="Email" type="email" />
  <PasswordField label="Password" showStrength />
  <Checkbox>I agree to the terms</Checkbox>
  <Button full>Create account</Button>
</form>
```

## 5. Pricing page
**3-tier grid + monthly/yearly toggle + comparison table + FAQ.**
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 items-stretch">
  {plans.map((p) => <PricingCard key={p.name} plan={p} yearly={yearly} />)}
</div>
```

## 6. Admin dashboard
**Sidebar + topbar + stats + data tables + activity feed.**
```tsx
<div className="min-h-screen flex">
  <Sidebar />
  <div className="flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col"><Topbar /><main className="p-6 space-y-6">{children}</main></div>
